Z||000007||HAGS||01-25-2001||08:56 PM||||Wouldnt start with my brother's explorer hooked up to it, sounded like it was cranking normally but it would start to get weaker on the 3rd or 4th crank after about 2-3 minutes of the explorer going at 2k RPMs.  We thought that it couldnt be the battery since I was using his in the jump start but why would it get weaker if his is good?||||reg||1
Z||000008||Indiana_resto_guy||01-25-2001||11:20 PM||||Have your starter checked for excessive amps while cranking. Change your starter.||||reg||1
Z||000009||firstfiero||01-26-2001||11:34 AM||||   Sometimes it can sound like your car is cranking properly....but their just not qiut enough juice to turn her over.. ||||reg||4
Z||000010||jerpro||01-27-2001||11:53 AM||||hmmm.... do a load test on your battery and test for the amperage. It should read around 230 amps.<BR>Also  the battery should be in 12.6 volts or higher to be 100% charged.<BR>A battery as low as 12.0 volts is only running at 25% efficiency. <BR>If the load test comes out faulty I would MAKE the store replace it for a new battery.<P>------------------<BR>Only try your best, and if at first you don't succeed... TRY HARDER.<p>[This message has been edited by jerpro (edited 01-27-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000011||HAGS||01-27-2001||11:59 AM||||ok, thanks, I'll try Autozone for the testing because I dont like nor trust the guys at the nearby shop.||||reg||1
Z||000012||jerpro||01-27-2001||12:18 PM||||If you can get the hands on a machine you could do it yourself. It is very simple.<BR>all you have to do is attach the testing alligator cables (usually the ones at the right of the machine) and plug the alternator clamp onto the + wires going to your engine from the battery, turn the car on at 2000 rev and turn the nob.<BR>then also do it with the car off.<BR>Also if you don't want to do it check the guy that is doing it. If the battery voltage after the nob is turned (load test) goes lower than 10.6 replace the battery, the minimum is 9.6 but I always go one volt higher (especially on fairly new batteries)<BR>hope this helps.<BR>||||reg||1
